### Centralized error contract (unit 5.9)
### Every gateway-produced error is application/problem+json with requestId. Passwords come from .env.

@gatewayUrl = http://localhost:8080

### 1. Login
# @name userLogin
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "demo-user",
  "password": "<DEMO_USER_PASSWORD from .env>"
}

@userToken = {{userLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 2. 404: no route. Body: title "Not Found", detail "No route matches this request.", requestId.
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/no-such-route
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### 3. 401: no token. Body keeps type urn:stockflow:problem:missing-token and has requestId.
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/products

### 4. 429: send request 5 many times at once. Body: title "Too Many Requests", requestId.
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/products
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### 5. 503: docker compose stop catalog, then send this. Body: title "Service Unavailable", requestId.
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/categories
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
